    Placeholder art for the UI, drawn as simple 24x24 shapes.

    To swap one for real art, drop a PNG at  Assets/UI/<key>.png
    e.g. the key "Menu/Inventory" is replaced by  Assets/UI/Menu/Inventory.png
    No code change needed: UiArt (Utils/UiArt.cs) uses the PNG when it exists,
    and falls back to the shape below otherwise.

    In XAML, art is used with  {utils:Art Menu/Inventory}
    In C#, with                UiArt.Get("Menu/Inventory")
-->
